    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26888" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lŏcellus</span></b> , i, m.
		dim.
		locus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a little place;</i> hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A compartment in a locker</i> or <i>chest</i>, Caes. ap. <i><span class="en">Charis. p.
			60</span></i> P.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praetorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					10, 88</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A chest, casket</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">anulos in locellum repositos haeredibus
					reddidit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Max. 7, 8, 9</span></i>
			.</div>
